    "minTurn": 15
  },
  "elevation": {
    "note": "90 m average and 20 m Gaussian, no opening (docs/track-data.md section 2.2), so Raidillon is not softened further. One targeted correction: along Kemmel (s 1325 to 2150 m) the surface model has a narrow bump of about 6 m at s 1400 to 1450 m followed by a flat (probably a structure or canopy over the track) and a smaller wiggle near s 2000 m; they put crests of -1.5 g and -0.6 g at 300 km/h on the straight. Over that span the profile is replaced by a cubic matching height and grade at both ends. A second on the descent to Pouhon (s 3400 to 3640 m): a 100 m ledge at about -4 % followed by -9.6 % (-0.7 g at 300 km/h) where the operator's labels give a steady -7.3 %. A third after Blanchimont (s 5900 to 6600 m): the surface model squeezes the climb to the Bus Stop into a 10 % step of 15 m over 150 m with a dip after it (+1.3 g and -1.2 g at 300 km/h), where the operator's altitude labels show a steady 2 to 3 %.",
    "openWindow": 0,
    "average": 90,
    "gradeSigma": 20,
    "publishedRange": 102.2,
    "rangeTolerance": 3.0,
    "corrections": [
      {
        "from": {
          "corner": 4,
          "offset": 157
        },
        "to": {
          "corner": 4,
          "offset": 982
        },
        "note": "Surface-model bump on early Kemmel (s 1400 to 1450 m, about 6 m) and wiggle near s 2000 m replaced by a cubic matching height and grade at both ends (estimate of the real smooth climb)."
      },
      {
        "from": {
          "corner": 9,
          "offset": 222
        },
        "to": {
          "corner": 10,
          "offset": -126
        },
        "note": "Surface-model ledge on the descent to Pouhon (about -4 % over s 3450 to 3550 m, then -9.6 %) replaced by a cubic matching height and grade at both ends. The operator's altitude labels give a steady -7.3 % from 438 m at 3110 m to 402 m at 3600 m."
      },
      {
        "from": {
          "corner": 16,
          "offset": 90
        },
        "to": {
          "corner": 18,
          "offset": -34
        },
        "note": "Surface-model step after Blanchimont (15 m over s 6050 to 6200 m, 10 %, then a dip; the stretch is lined with forest) replaced by a cubic matching height and grade at both ends. The circuit operator's altitude labels give a steady 2 to 3 % climb here: 388 m at 5700 m, 398 m at 6000 m, 408 m at 6540 m, 418 m at the line."
      }
    ]
  },
